  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\n～に{没頭|ぼっとう}する (to be absorbed in ~)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {仕事|しごと}に{没頭|ぼっとう}する (to be absorbed in work)\n- {研究|けんきゅう}に{没頭|ぼっとう}する (to be immersed in research)\n- {勉強|べんきょう}に{没頭|ぼっとう}する (to be absorbed in studying)\n- {読書|どくしょ}に{没頭|ぼっとう}する (to be absorbed in reading)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {夢中|むちゅう}になる: To be crazy about, absorbed in — more emotional and colloquial. Can be used for entertainment and fun activities more naturally.\n- {集中|しゅうちゅう}する: To concentrate — more deliberate and controlled. {没頭|ぼっとう} implies losing oneself, while {集中|しゅうちゅう} implies focused effort.\n- {熱中|ねっちゅう}する: To be enthusiastic about — emphasizes passion and excitement rather than deep focus.",
